    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="age_country_gender_reach_breakdown" id="id-d663f9e4711840f7a754817d648920b6" profiles="id-6f2b40d3c8b743e288ae40a33bba56a0">
      <property key="ads_id" value="String @db.VarChar(64)"/>
      <property key="ads" value="ads @relation(fields: [ads_id], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)"/>
      <property key="location_code" value="String @db.VarChar(10)"/>
      <property key="location" value="location @relation(fields: [location_code], references: [code], onDelete: Restrict)"/>
      <property key="age_range" value="String @db.VarChar(50)"/>
      <property key="male" value="Int?"/>
      <property key="female" value="Int?"/>
      <property key="unknown" value="Int?"/>
      <property key="pk_ads_age_country_gender_reach_breakdown" value="@@id([ads_id, location_code, age_range], map: &quot;pk_ads_age_country_gender_reach_breakdown&quot;)"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="location" id="id-126ea3cdd7794fee9b71a326c25016d1" profiles="id-ab6b4c8086a64fcd8398dedec961c020">
      <documentation>The Location entity serves as a unified geographic master catalog designed to standardize and normalize geographic target identifiers returned by the Meta Ads Library API. It aggregates multiple classification standards—ranging from sovereign states to multi-national economic blocks and geographic regions—into a single, queryable model.

Standardization &amp; Multi-Norm Support: It accommodates international standards such as ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 (e.g., GB, US, CO) and ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 (e.g., GBR, USA, COL) alongside Meta-specific or non-ISO regional and economic group identifiers (e.g., EU for European Union, LATAM, or broader trade/geographical blocks).

Categorization &amp; Lineage Tracking: By capturing location_type (e.g., COUNTRY, REGION, BLOCK, UNKNOWN) and code_standard (e.g., ISO_3166_1_ALPHA_2, META_REGIONAL), the entity enforces strict type classification while preserving the source provenance and governing rule of each code.

Relational Integrity: It functions as a single source of truth for cross-referencing reach metrics, targeting parameters, and location-based performance data, ensuring database resiliency against unannounced API updates or non-standard region representations.</documentation>
      <property key="code" value="String @id @db.VarChar(10)"/>
      <property key="location_name" value="String @db.VarChar(100)"/>
      <property key="location_type" value="LocationTypeEnum @default(UNKNOWN)"/>
      <property key="code_standard" value="String @db.VarChar(100)"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="languages" id="id-afbd17dc5aeb4a319c139cd79412f5b8" profiles="id-ab6b4c8086a64fcd8398dedec961c020">
      <property key="code" value="String @id @db.VarChar(3)"/>
      <property key="language_name" value="String @db.VarChar(100)"/>
      <property key="code_standard" value="String @db.VarChar(100)"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="ads_languages" id="id-6e41b60a9a024ba8ba21b6f3e1d2e58c" profiles="id-da0ce2dce1084d86a6374d36756bcf1e">
